1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
If you're going to Europe this fall, please don't pack the same wardrobe for Milano, Paris

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:04,920
and London.

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:07,760
Three fashion capitals, but they have three completely different dress codes.

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:12,000
Starting with Paris, here I would pack less and focus on pieces that they work together.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Think of trench or long wool coat, or straight leg denim, ballet flats or pair of loafers.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,559
One good bag that works every day.

7
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:19,559
Hear me out.

8
00:00:19,559 --> 00:00:21,160
Keep the colors understated.

9
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:24,280
Think of black, grey, burgundy, navy and cream.

10
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,520
The goal is not to look over styled, it's slightly undone, like I just threw this on

11
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,600
even when you did not.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,840
For Milano, I'm immediately dressing things up.

13
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:36,200
I would bring tailored trousers, fitness, a beautiful coat or a leather jacket.

14
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,840
Definitely stronger shoes.

15
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:42,840
Also don't forget here, it's where you can play more with accessories, jewelries, richer

16
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:45,320
colors like chocolate brown, deep red.

17
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:49,160
Look, as an Italian, the only thing that I can say is start with your shoes and then

18
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,160
build everything up.

19
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:53,799
If you're going specifically to Milano, bear in mind it's way more polished and intentional.

20
00:00:53,799 --> 00:00:59,040
London, in my opinion, it's where you experiment, where you literally get your personality out.

21
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,759
But don't forget, we have all the seasons in one day, so definitely bring with you a

22
00:01:02,759 --> 00:01:03,759
coat.

23
00:01:03,759 --> 00:01:07,959
I would personally pack a brown jacket, knitwear, relaxed trousers, definitely your most comfortable

24
00:01:07,959 --> 00:01:09,559
sneakers because you walk a lot.

25
00:01:09,559 --> 00:01:15,160
This is where I would have more fun mixing vintage, checks, leather or something unexpected.

26
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,160
This is only my starter pack.

27
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:22,519
I will break down exactly what to pack city by city, so tell me, Paris, London or Milan,

28
00:01:22,519 --> 00:01:23,519
which one are you packing for?

29
00:01:23,519 --> 00:01:24,519
That's all for today.

30
00:01:24,519 --> 00:01:25,519
Thank you for listening.

